From 1322426bf2450c29d39c0391d66cb519396db1c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:39:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Option --displacement-gradient of the cermet and of the
 polycrystal

The option gives the displacement gradient H = F - I instead of the
deformation gradient to the behaviours (parameter DisplacementGradient
of mfem-mgis).

The macroscopic unknowns of UniaxialMacroscopicStressPeriodicSimulation
are now the diagonal components of the macroscopic displacement
gradient, and the imposed axial loading is given as Hzz. The
macroscopic gradients given to mfem-mgis are H with the option, F = I + H
otherwise. In single precision, H keeps the precision of the
macroscopic strain, and the resolution of the fixed point on the
lateral stresses, computed on the gradients given to mfem-mgis, becomes
negligible.

The metallic interface of the cermet, written in the Hencky strain
framework, computes its strain without cancellation. The grains,
written with the deformation gradient, receive F = I + H.

The tests CermetNullStrainXXYY-DisplacementGradient and
UniaxialPolycrystalTest-DisplacementGradient run the two cases with the
option, compared with Cast3M as without it.
